  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 alternating stack on Fused Silica substrate for 1550nm bandpass filtering. Layers 1-8 (Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs) fixed at thicknesses [158.5, 268.4, 158.3, 268.2, 158.1, 268.0, 157.9, 267.9] nm from iteration 02 baseline. Layers 9-20 initialized at mean thickness from iterations 06, 13, and 17 candidates, optimized within ±15nm absolute bounds. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with curvature penalty term penalizing |d[i+1] - 2*d[i] + d[i-1]| > 5nm. Evaluate transmittance at normal incidence, unpolarized. Score objectives: maximize mean T at 1550nm (weight 1.0), minimize mean T in 1400-1500nm (weight 0.5), minimize mean T in 1600-1700nm (weight 0.5). Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
